# selfdef auditd-immutable — enforce profile.
#
#   -e 2   — audit enabled, RULES IMMUTABLE until reboot.
#
# Once loaded (next augenrules --load OR daemon restart), the
# kernel REFUSES every subsequent auditctl modification:
#   - `auditctl -d <rule>` → exit 1 "audit_set_enabled: rejected"
#   - `auditctl -D` → exit 1
#   - `auditctl -e 0` → exit 1
#   - `augenrules --load` of a NEW rule file → kernel ignores
#     the load attempt; rules stay as-they-were-at-immutability
#
# Only a REBOOT can undo. This is the strongest defense against
# an attacker who lands root + tries to silence audit detection
# (audit-rules + auditd-tune + selfdef-collector-auditd) before
# operator notices.
#
# Operator-pull rule changes follow the procedure:
#   1. Edit /etc/audit/rules.d/<file>.rules
#   2. Reboot the host
#   3. Verify with `auditctl -s | grep enabled` (expect 2)

-e 2
